==English==
{{wikipedia|Iceberg (disambiguation)|Iceberg}}
[[File:Ice-floe params hg.png|thumb|Iceberg diagram]]
[[Image:Iceberg upernavik 2007-08-11 1.jpg|thumb|250px|An iceberg]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|nl|ijsberg}} (compound of {{com|nl|ijs|t1=ice|berg|t2=mountain|nocat=1}}), from {{der|en|dum|ijsberch}}. First used to describe a glacier as seen at a distance from a ship then used as a term to describe the floating chunks of ice broken off from such glaciers. Cognate to {{cog|de|Eisberg}}, {{cog|da|isbjerg}}, {{cog|no|isberg}} and {{cog|sv|isberg}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈaɪsbɜːɡ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈaɪsbɝɡ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-iceberg.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪsbɜː(ɹ)ɡ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ice|berg}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The seaward end of a glacier. {{century|18|19}}
# A huge mass of ocean-floating [[ice]] which has broken off a [[glacier]] or [[ice shelf]] {{century|19}}
#: {{ux|en|The Titanic hit an '''iceberg''' and sank.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} An [[aloof]] [[person]]. {{century|19}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|after an adjective}} An [[impending]] [[disastrous]] [[event]] whose adverse [[effect]]s are only beginning to show, in reference to one-tenth of the [[volume]] of an iceberg being visible above [[water]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|work=The Economist|url=http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21590476-how-barack-obama-can-get-least-some-his-credibility-back-man-who-used-walk-water|title=How Barack Obama can get at least some of his credibility back|passage=He has little to lose: at present he will go down in history, alongside George W. Bush, as a skipper who ignored the looming '''fiscal iceberg'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|slang|chiefly|Internet slang}} A [[topic]] that is more [[convoluted]] and [[fractal]] than it may seem at first, and is therefore difficult to grasp in its entirety.
#: {{nearsyn|en|rabbit hole}}
#: {{ux|en|Do some digging into that politician's past life and associates, and you'll see that the '''iceberg''' runs deep.}}
#: {{ux|en|There's a massive '''iceberg''' of increasingly crazy [[fanfic]]s out there based around those two characters.}}

